      "text": [
        "اَ «مَا خَرَجَ مِنْ طَرَفَيْكَ اَلْأَسْفَلَيْنِ اَلذَّكَرِ وَ اَلدُّبُرِ مِنْ غَائِطٍ أَوْ بَوْلٍ أَوْ مَنِيٍّ أَوْ رِيحٍ وَ اَلنَّوْمُ حَتَّى يُذْهِبَ اَلْعَقْلَ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.137 - Zurarah ibn A'yan asked Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) and Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) about what nullifies wudu (ablution).\nThey said: \"Anything that exits from your two lower openings, the front (urethra) and the back (anus), such as excrement, urine, semen, or wind, as well as sleep that causes a loss of consciousness, invalidates wudu”."
        ]
      }
